<% content_for :title, "Percentage Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Percentage calculator page (spec issue #31, DESIGN.md BLEND). A multi-mode
  calculator: the main mode picker selects the operation; only that mode's inputs show.
  The form posts over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works
  without JS (server validates the selected mode). Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input
  column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to one column on mobile.

  Mode-picker rule (the picker-rule sweep): a mode picker is always a native radio
  <fieldset>; presentation follows N + label length. The main picker has FIVE
  multi-word modes (N ≥ 4 / multi-word) → the "selectable option list" (.mode-option):
  one bordered, divided container, each row = a radio glyph + the bold mode label + a
  one-line helper naming what it computes. The Increase|Decrease sub-toggle, by
  contrast, is N = 2 short labels → it stays a segmented control (unchanged).

  Spacing scale (DESIGN.md §3, "targets not minimums"):
    • stacked fields → space-y-5
    • major blocks within the card (mode → fields → submit) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Math</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Percentage Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Five percentage operations in one place — what is P% of a number, what percent one
    number is of another, percent-of-what, the difference between two numbers, and an
    increase or decrease. Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/percentage", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "percentage" } do |f| %>

      <%# Main mode picker — "selectable option list" (.mode-option), per the picker rule:
          FIVE multi-word modes (N ≥ 4 / multi-word) → one bordered, divided container of
          full-width rows, NOT N wrapping chips. The accessible control is unchanged: a
          radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[mode], each radio visually-hidden
          (peer sr-only) and paired to a styled <label for>; the active row is painted
          with no JS via peer:checked, and a real radio glyph (.mode-option::before) is
          the non-colour active cue (DESIGN.md §6). Each row names the operation (label)
          and, on a helper line, what that mode computes. %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Mode</legend>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-[13px] border border-border-input divide-y divide-rule">
          <% [
               ["percent_of",      "Percent of a number",  "What is P% of a number"],
               ["what_percent",    "What percent",         "What percent one number is of another"],
               ["percent_of_what", "Percent of what",      "A number is P% of what whole"],
               ["difference",      "Percentage difference", "The percent difference between two numbers"],
               ["change",          "Increase / decrease",  "Apply a P% increase or decrease to a number"]
             ].each_with_index do |(value, text, helper), i| %>
            <div>
              <%= f.radio_button :mode, value,
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { percentage_target: "modeInput", action: "percentage#select" } %>
              <%= f.label :mode, value: value,
                    class: "mode-option",
                    data: { percentage_target: "pill", mode: value } do %>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink"><%= text %></span>
                <span class="text-xs text-muted"><%= helper %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Per-mode fields. Each block declares the modes it serves; Stimulus shows only
          the active mode's blocks and disables the rest so they aren't submitted.
          Stacked tier: space-y-5 down the column (DESIGN.md §3). %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# V1 — every mode %>
        <div data-percentage-target="field"
             data-percentage-modes="percent_of what_percent percent_of_what difference change">
          <%= f.label :v1, "Value (V1)", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_v1" %>
          <%= f.number_field :v1, id: "inputs_v1", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                placeholder: "0", class: "field-input mt-1.5" %>
        </div>

        <%# V2 — what_percent, difference %>
        <div data-percentage-target="field"
             data-percentage-modes="what_percent difference">
          <%= f.label :v2, "Value (V2)", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_v2" %>
          <%= f.number_field :v2, id: "inputs_v2", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                placeholder: "0", class: "field-input mt-1.5" %>
        </div>

        <%# Percent — percent_of, percent_of_what, change. % affix on the Affix tier. %>
        <div data-percentage-target="field"
             data-percentage-modes="percent_of percent_of_what change">
          <%= f.label :percent, "Percent (P)", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_percent" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :percent, id: "inputs_percent", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Direction toggle — change only (the increase/decrease segmented control). %>
        <div data-percentage-target="field" data-percentage-field="change"
             data-percentage-modes="change">
          <span class="field-label">Direction</span>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex gap-1 rounded-[11px] border border-border-input bg-bg p-1">
            <% [["increase", "Increase"], ["decrease", "Decrease"]].each_with_index do |(value, text), i| %>
              <%= f.radio_button :direction, value,
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { action: "percentage#selectDirection" } %>
              <%= f.label :direction, text, value: value,
                    class: "direction-pill",
                    data: { percentage_target: "directionPill" } %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
